Description: open-source motion graphics and compositing editor
 EffectCraft is a native motion graphics and visual effects compositor
 written in Rust. It has layers with keyframes and a graph editor, masks and
 shapes, text animators, expressions, 3D cameras and lights, a large library of
 effects and a render queue (H.264, HEVC, AV1, ProRes, WebM and image
 sequences), and it composites on the GPU (wgpu).
 .
 The headless renderer, command runner and MCP server that drive the same
 editor commands are in the storytold-effectcraft-cli package.

Package: storytold-effectcraft-cli
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Suggests: storytold-effectcraft (= ${binary:Version}),
         storytold-craft-fonts,
Enhances: storytold-effectcraft,
Description: headless renderer, command runner and MCP server for the EffectCraft editor
 effectcraft-cli runs EffectCraft's editor commands without a window: it
 summarises a project, runs commands from a list or a script, reads and sets
 layer properties, renders frames and compositions, and runs After
 Effects-style JavaScript.
 .
 effectcraft-cli mcp starts an MCP server on standard input and output, so that
 an AI agent can drive the editor engine, headless or attached to a running
 EffectCraft window. It has no windowing or GPU dependencies. The
 storytold-effectcraft package provides the editor window.
